      "id": "ftbxqzs",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Economics"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economics originates from the Greek word 'Oikonomia', which translates to household management.",
        "The discipline is divided into Microeconomics (study of individual units) and Macroeconomics (study of the economy as a whole).",
        "The four essential factors of production are Land, Labour, Capital, and Entrepreneurship.",
        "Scarcity arises because human wants are unlimited while resources available to satisfy them are limited.",
        "Opportunity cost measures the value of the next best alternative forgone when a choice is made."
      ],
      "id": "wwjt8ys"
    },
